    "metadata": {
      "name": "EventGraph",
      "description": "Player health and score with win/lose rules.",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "created_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "ADVANCED 8/9: A SMALL COMPLETE GAME - pickups, score, health\nThree classes cooperate only through events, never through references:\n  AdvPlayerStats (on the player): health, score, win and lose.\n  AdvPickup (on every coin/medkit): on overlap it SENDS `AdvPlayerStats.add_score` or `.heal`\n     to whoever touched it, then removes itself.\n  AdvHazard (spikes): on overlap it applies engine damage; AdvPlayerStats listens to the engine's Damage event.\nCompile order: a class that sends another class's event needs that class compiled first (the Send node\nreads the other class's compiled events), so Compile All builds AdvPlayerStats before AdvPickup.",
        "position": [
          0,
          -360
        ],
        "size": [
          1500,
          260
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.75,
          0.2,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "1. START - report the starting health. Variable defaults (health 100, score 0, win_score 50) come from the\nVariables panel, so a level can override them per player.",
        "position": [
          -40,
          -80
        ],
        "size": [
          1020,
          500
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.45,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "bp",
          "bp_hp",
          "bp_cat",
          "bp_log"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "2. SCORING - a pickup sends `add_score(points)`. Add it, and when the total reaches `win_score` end the\ngame as a WIN. Rules live in the player so every pickup stays tiny.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          620
        ],
        "size": [
          2360,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "as",
          "as_s",
          "as_add",
          "as_set",
          "as_win",
          "as_won",
          "as_if",
          "as_end"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-4",
        "text": "3. HEALING - add the amount but never exceed `max_health` (Min of the sum and the cap). The\nsame Min/Max pattern guards every bounded stat.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          1310
        ],
        "size": [
          1680,
          710
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.35,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "hl",
          "hl_hp",
          "hl_add",
          "hl_cap",
          "hl_max",
          "hl_set"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-5",
        "text": "4. DAMAGE - the ENGINE event `Damage` (raised by hazards through game::apply_damage) arrives on this\nobject. Every hit costs 20 health; at zero or below the game is lost. (The event carries a float\n`amount`; this simple rule ignores it and uses a flat 20.)",
        "position": [
          -30,
          2230
        ],
        "size": [
          2360,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.8,
          0.3,
          0.3,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "dm",
          "dm_hp",
          "dm_sub",
          "dm_set",
          "dm_dead",
          "dm_if",
          "dm_end"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-6",
        "text": "5. END OF GAME - `game_over(won)` can be raised twice (a coin and a spike in one frame). A `finished`\nflag guards it: only the first call logs the result; `Select String` picks the message from the bool.",
        "position": [
          -30,
          2920
        ],
        "size": [
          2360,
          480
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.45,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "go",
          "go_done",
          "go_not",
          "go_if",
          "go_set",
          "go_msg",
          "go_log"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "custom_event_defs": {}
  },
